// EN translation FIRST PASS. Literary editorial approval outstanding.
const OUTCOMES_EN_E001_E050 = Object.freeze({"E001.1":{"s":"The merchants count the broken spokes first, then stare in astonishment at the repaired wheels. Their foreman pays without haggling, desperate to get the caravan moving."},"E001.2":{"s":"Faced with an armed party, the merchants surrender a portion of their cargo. The price of your persistence jingles in the purse.","f":"The merchants raise the alarm, and the dispute over their cargo ends with drawn steel. A skirmish lies ahead."},"E001.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} arranges the wagons in a half-circle and orders the extra fires put out; the raiders leave empty-handed. The merchants share their gold and provisions.","f":"At dawn the bandits slip through the unfinished barricade. Steel must answer them: a skirmish begins."},"E001.4":{"s":"You leave the caravan at the crossroads. The merchants watch you go in silence, their hands still resting on their sword hilts."},"E002.1":{"s":"The soldiers sell you some of their travelling rations, then divide the proceeds around the campfire. As you leave, one asks you not to give their names to the patrol."},"E002.2":{"s":"One deserter silently casts his old regimental badge into the fire and takes his place beneath your banner. The others look away rather than betray their envy.","f":"The soldiers refuse to part with their comrade without payment and take some of the party's gold. You leave their fire with no new companion.","v":{"rs":"The deserter is ready to exchange his regimental badge for the royal standard, but there is no place for him in the party. He leaves you gold in farewell."}},"E002.3":{"s":"The patrol accepts the deserters and pays the reward without asking questions. The coins sound unpleasantly loud as the prisoners are led away.","f":"The deserters realise whom you intend to hand them over to and reach for their weapons. A skirmish erupts in the clearing."},"E002.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} leads the soldiers along a trail the patrol would miss even in broad daylight. The former soldiers share their supplies before parting.","f":"The soldiers hesitate at the fork, afraid to follow {{heroName}} into the unknown. In the end, they return to their campfire."},"E003.1":{"s":"The silver chain rings plaintively as you raise the bucket. The water is pure, and the party replenishes its supplies.","f":"The water is colder than ice, and the warning on the chain proves no idle threat. {{affectedHeroName}} collapses beside the well, gravely wounded by an unseen force.","v":{"nf":"The silver chain jerks beneath the icy water, but none of the eligible fighters suffers a grave wound. You let go of the bucket."}},"E003.2":{"s":"The coins vanish into the depths with a brief silver chime. The bucket returns filled with clean water, fit for the long road ahead."},"E003.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} recites the words of purification over the well, and the silver chain falls still. The party fills its flasks without fear.","f":"The chain lashes against the stone rim, shattering the filled vessels. Some of the supplies are lost."},"E003.4":{"s":"You leave the well untouched, its silver chain reflecting your departing party long after you have gone. No one asks exactly what the word “debt” means."},"E004.1":{"s":"You question the witnesses one by one until the contradictions become impossible to ignore. The grateful peasants reward your judgement with gold.","f":"The crowd does not want to hear new evidence and demands an immediate verdict. To get people out of the crush, you have to give up some of the gold."},"E004.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} makes each side speak in turn, and the court finally reaches a verdict without mob justice. The village headman pays gold for keeping the peace.","f":"Some in the crowd denounce {{heroName}}'s verdict as a fraud and rush to free the accused. A skirmish erupts on the road."},"E004.3":{"s":"You break through the guards and lead the prisoner out of the crowd. Before long, a new companion joins your party.","f":"The peasants mistake the liberation attempt for an attack and call together a neighboring garrison. Instead of a trial, a battle begins.","v":{"rs":"The prisoner is free, but there is no room for him in your party. He rewards his rescuers with gold and goes his own way."}},"E004.4":{"s":"You pass the road where the peasants are still arguing over a bound man's guilt. Behind you, someone demands a verdict."},"E005.1":{"s":"The coins go to the toll collectors and the chain is lowered across the bridge. No one undertakes to check the suspicious seal."},"E005.2":{"s":"You manage to discover an incorrect signature on the order, and the collectors return the illegal part of the fee. A few coins enter the treasury.","f":"The baron's people declare that it is possible to argue with the order only for an additional fee. An attempt to defend the right costs the party gold."},"E005.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} compares the impression with the entries in the register: the seal is forged. The toll collectors return the gold rather than face the real baron.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a discrepancy, but the evidence is insufficient. The collectors close the register and wait for the next traveler."},"E005.4":{"s":"You take the bridge with a quick dash, and the collectors do not dare to pursue the party. The payment remains with you.","f":"The chain is stretched across the road, and armed people emerge from the guardhouse. The breakthrough turns into a skirmish."},"E006.1":{"s":"You bandage the knight and give him water. When the pain subsides, he swears to march beneath your banner. A new companion joins your party.","v":{"rs":"The knight recovers enough to swear an oath, but there is no room for him in your party. He rewards you with gold for saving his life."}},"E006.2":{"s":"You find gold in the knight's heraldic chest. He is too weak to object as the party takes the spoils.","f":"People with the same coat of arms appear on the road and mistake you for robbers. The confrontation begins without any opportunity to explain."},"E006.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds traces of his pursuers and forces them to give up the chase. The bags found contain gold.","f":"There are far more pursuers than the boot prints suggested. The confrontation escalates into a battle."},"E006.4":{"s":"You leave the knight by the side of the road along with the coat of arms chest. In the distance, the footsteps of his pursuers are heard getting closer."},"E007.1":{"s":"A voice in the depths of the grove stops listing names and points to a safe path. Supplies left by previous travelers are found on it.","f":"The melodious names give way to a sharp cry, and {{affectedHeroName}} falls among the roots with a serious wound. The trees instantly fall silent.","v":{"nf":"The singing grove interrupts the melody with a piercing cry, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The trees fall silent."}},"E007.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} pronounces the ancient words without a single mistake, and the grove responds with a friendly rustle. The elves give you gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} mispronounces a single word. The grove echoes the mistake again and again until the party retreats."},"E007.3":{"s":"The luminous branch breaks off with a dry crack, and its core turns out to be more valuable than gold. The party receives a reward for rare wood.","f":"The grove responds with a lashing of intertwined branches as elven guards emerge from the trees. A skirmish begins."},"E007.4":{"s":"You skirt the grove by a rocky path, spending supplies on the longer journey. The trees' songs follow you long after you leave."},"E008.1":{"s":"You help the hunters drive the beast into a narrow gorge and overpower it. The elves pay you in gold.","f":"The monster breaks through the beaters and gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}. The hunters withdraw the party from the forest.","v":{"nf":"The monster breaks through the hunting enclosure, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The hunters retreat without prey."}},"E008.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} reaches the narrow pass before the beast, allowing the hunters to cut off its escape. They reward the clever trap with gold.","f":"The monster finds a hidden trail and bursts straight into your path. A skirmish begins."},"E008.3":{"s":"You get to the prize ahead of the elves and claim the valuable trophy. By the time you return, it has been sold for gold.","f":"The hunters discover your attempt to steal their trophy and turn their entire hunting band against you. A battle breaks out."},"E008.4":{"s":"You refuse to go hunting, and the elves return to the trail without reproach. A few minutes later the forest is again filled with the sounds of the chase."},"E009.1":{"s":"The merchant weighs out the provisions and seals the bargain with a remarkably thin silver coin. By dawn, the purchased supplies are stowed in your wagons."},"E009.2":{"s":"The dice fall in your favour. The merchant counts out your winnings with a rueful smile, and the coins swell your treasury.","f":"The merchant wins the final throw and pockets your stake. At the next stall, someone is already offering you a rematch."},"E009.3":{"s":"The mercenary listens to the proposal, extinguishes his lantern and goes under your banner. The party now has one more companion.","f":"The mercenary asks for payment for negotiations, and then hides between the shops. The party loses some of its gold.","v":{"rs":"The mercenary is ready to leave the moonlit market for the road, but there is no room for him in your party. He leaves you gold in place of a contract."}},"E009.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} unearths a forgotten clause in the market charter, forcing the trader to lower the price. You leave with extra supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} tries to reduce the price, but the elf only turns over the hourglass. The trade ends without profit."},"E009.5":{"s":"You leave the lunar market before dawn. When you look around, there are no longer any lights or stalls between the trees."},"E010.1":{"s":"The duelist recognizes your victory and hands over the required gold at the walls of the old tower. The black arrow remains stuck in the oak bark.","f":"Your challenger is faster than the note led you to believe. {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded, and the referee calls an end to the duel.","v":{"nf":"The duelist delivers a dangerous blow, but none of the available fighters is gravely wounded. The referee interrupts the fight."}},"E010.2":{"s":"You approach the tower with your whole party, and the challenger abandons his ruse. He pays you in gold.","f":"The challenger brings his fighters, and instead of a single duel, a skirmish begins."},"E010.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} accepts the one-on-one challenge and emerges victorious, receiving gold according to the terms of the duel.","f":"The duelist finds a gap in {{heroName}}'s defenses, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The fight is stopped.","v":{"nf":"The enemy finds a gap in the defense, but none of the available fighters is gravely wounded. The duel ends without victory."}},"E010.4":{"s":"You break the black arrow and leave a note under the roots of the oak tree. The abandoned tower will never know if you accepted the challenge."},"E011.1":{"s":"The elves gratefully accept your flasks and carry the chest through the scorched earth. They pay in gold for the saved seeds."},"E011.2":{"s":"You give some of the water, and the elven guardians divide it for the last days of the journey. In response, they count out the gold."},"E011.3":{"s":"The keepers agree to pay before you make way for their chest. The gold is yours.","f":"The elves clutch the chest's handles and refuse to talk about payment until the seeds are saved. You part ways without a deal."},"E011.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} picks up the heavy chest, not allowing a single seed to spill onto the scorched earth. Grateful guardians give out gold and supplies.","f":"The chest is heavier than it appears, and {{heroName}} has to stop. The keepers carry on without your help."},"E012.1":{"s":"You surface with coins while the reflection of someone else's future lingers on the lake. The gold goes into your treasury.","f":"It is not a reflection that rises from the depths, but something capable of dragging the living along with it. {{affectedHeroName}} dies before the party can come to the rescue.","v":{"nf":"Underwater, something grabs your legs, but among the available fighters, no one dies. The treasure remains at the bottom."}},"E012.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} reads the images on the water and notices the path to the surviving supplies of the former travelers. The party takes supplies.","f":"The mirror surface shows too many different roads, and {{heroName}} chooses the wrong one. Part of the reserves is spent searching for a way out."},"E012.3":{"s":"The stone breaks the reflection, and the lake throws gold coins to the shore. The party quickly collects them.","f":"Instead of circles, there are cracks in the water, and guards of the lake rise from the depths. A skirmish begins."},"E012.4":{"s":"You pass by a lake where the future looks more convincing than the present. The water never returns its usual reflection to you."},"E013.1":{"s":"Before the entire clan, the chieftain acknowledges your victory and orders your hard-won trophy brought forth. You claim its value in gold.","f":"In the stone circle, the enemy turns out to be stronger, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The orcs remove the winner from the circle amid shouts of approval.","v":{"nf":"In the stone circle, the opponent delivers the decisive blow, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The orcs declare the test failed."}},"E013.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} withstands the blow so that even the orc spectators fall silent for a moment. The leader gives the promised reward in gold.","f":"The shield cannot withstand everything: {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The leader declares the test over.","v":{"nf":"The powerful blow knocks down the shield, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The leader does not count the test."}},"E013.3":{"s":"The leader responds to the insult with laughter and throws you a gold stake as a reward for your courage.","f":"The orc leader stops laughing and calls the entire clan to defend their honor. The battle begins."},"E013.4":{"s":"You leave the orcs to their stone circle and tests of strength. The leader does not try to hold the party."},"E014.1":{"s":"The orcs accept food in place of coin and let you cross the ford without argument. Your provision packs are lighter now."},"E014.2":{"s":"The elder at the ford takes your gold and orders the crossing opened. The orcs clearly find the bargain strange, but they keep their word.","f":"The orcs reject the coins and demand the customary food. The argument quickly turns into a fight."},"E014.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} enters into an exchange according to clan rules, transferring agreed upon coins and supplies. The orcs let the party through the ford.","f":"A second toll collector interrupts {{heroName}}'s negotiations and demands another payment. No agreement can be reached."},"E014.4":{"s":"You rush through the ford before the orcs have time to deploy a barrier. The party goes to the other side.","f":"Halfway across the ford, the clan warriors close ranks and refuse to let you force a passage. A battle begins."},"E015.1":{"s":"The orc smiths hand over the provisions you paid for, with a warning not to touch the hot anvils. Your wagons carry the new supplies."},"E015.2":{"s":"You help deliver ore to the forge, and the blacksmiths give you supplies as a reward.","f":"On the way, the cart with ore gets stuck, and the party’s own supplies are spent on pulling out the cargo."},"E015.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} repairs the gate, after which the heavy ingots rise again without effort. The blacksmiths give you gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} notices a crack in the support beam and stops work until repairs are made. The blacksmiths thank you for your caution, but do not give you a reward."},"E015.4":{"s":"You quietly take the box out of the forge and find supplies in it. The blacksmiths are too busy with the forge to raise the alarm.","f":"The watchman notices the missing box, and the clan masters grab their weapons. A skirmish begins."},"E016.1":{"s":"The orcs take the gold and unlock the captive's chains. He joins your party, bringing a share of his travelling provisions.","v":{"rs":"The standard-bearer is freed, but there is no place for him in your party. He gives you gold and continues his journey alone."}},"E016.2":{"s":"You scatter the escort and free the standard-bearer. He joins your party on the road.","f":"The orc guards manage to close ranks and draw their weapons. A skirmish begins.","v":{"rs":"The escort is beaten and the standard-bearer freed, but there is no room for him in your party. He leaves gold in gratitude instead."}},"E016.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} distracts the convoy while the prisoner's chains are removed. A new companion appears in your party.","f":"One of the guards notices movement at the shackles and raises the alarm; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded during the retreat.","v":{"rs":"The chains are off, but the freed standard-bearer has no place in your ranks. He leaves you gold in thanks.","nf":"The guards notice the attempt to remove the shackles, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The standard bearer remains in custody."}},"E016.4":{"s":"You pass by a convoy, and the standard bearer continues to march, guarded by orcs. His promise of reward is drowned in the noise of footsteps."},"E017.1":{"s":"The shaman takes the gold and reads the nearest danger from the pattern of the bones. In addition to the prediction, he gives out supplies for the journey."},"E017.2":{"s":"You beat the shaman at his own game and take the gold prize.","f":"The shaman smiles as the last bone lands on the wrong side. The party loses the agreed upon coins."},"E017.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} points out a flaw in the shaman's reading and demands a new interpretation. Before the witnesses, the orc pays up in gold.","f":"The shaman declares the objection an insult to the spirits, and the argument escalates into a skirmish."},"E017.4":{"s":"You leave the shaman with his carved bones. His last prediction remains unheard."},"E018.1":{"s":"The caravan manages to turn around before the arrival of the orcish party and rewards you with gold.","f":"The warning comes too late: the orcs intercept the messenger right at the carts. A skirmish begins."},"E018.2":{"s":"You set up an ambush on the edge of a ravine and force the orcs to retreat, leaving behind some of the provisions.","f":"The orcs discover traces of the ambush before dawn and change their route. The party returns without any loot."},"E018.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} lays a false trail along the stones, and the orcs move away from the caravan. In gratitude, the merchants give supplies.","f":"The orcs see through the false trail and turn their entire warband against you. The attempted ruse ends in a battle."},"E018.4":{"s":"You do not interfere with the orcs' campaign. The red drum thunders in the gorge for a long time until the caravan disappears around the bend."},"E019.1":{"s":"The cart stops, and under the canvas a purse of gold is found, which you take.","f":"Armed undead rise from under the canvas and attack those who stopped the cart. A skirmish begins."},"E019.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} completes an unfinished funeral rite; the canvas falls onto the empty boards. The party receives gold and supplies.","f":"A cursed force bursts out from under the canvas, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The cart continues its journey without a driver.","v":{"nf":"A cursed force bursts out from under the canvas, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The cart continues to roll without a driver."}},"E019.3":{"s":"The flames destroy the cart, and among the charred remains you find gold coins.","f":"The fire dies on the wet boards, and the driverless cart keeps rolling. You are forced to retreat."},"E019.4":{"s":"You pass a cart without a driver and do not touch its load. The creaking of wheels subsides around the bend, and under the canvas someone continues to move."},"E020.1":{"s":"The skeleton accepts the gold fee, carefully counting the coins with his bony fingers. The cemetery gate creaks, letting the party through."},"E020.2":{"s":"The collector agrees to a lower duty and puts some of the coins into a hole in his cloak. The road is open.","f":"The skeleton declares the discount an insult to the dead and demands payment in full. The party parts with a considerable sum of gold."},"E020.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} requires a receipt on the royal form, and the collector returns the gold without finding a suitable seal.","f":"The skeleton throws the form at his feet and calls for the cemetery guards. A skirmish begins."},"E020.4":{"s":"The Collector raises his weapon as soon as the party approaches the outpost. The fight begins right between the old tombstones.","f":"The skeleton gives way and the party leaves the outpost behind without further conflict."},"E021.1":{"s":"The officer listens to the story of the long-dead army and finally lowers the ghostly staff. Supplies remain at the site of his disappearance.","f":"The ghost mistakes the words for an enemy lie, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded by an invisible blade.","v":{"nf":"The phantom commander draws his blade, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. You fail to convince him of the truth."}},"E021.2":{"s":"You repeat the old order, and the officer solemnly hands over the army's long-guarded chest. Its gold joins your reserves.","f":"The ghost demands a drill review and calls his dead subordinates from the darkness. A skirmish begins."},"E021.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} completes the oath that the officer was unable to fulfill during his lifetime, and he disappears with a sigh of relief. The reward is gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} says the final words, but the ghost continues to repeat the same command. The ritual does not bring peace."},"E021.4":{"s":"You leave the officer issuing orders to invisible troops. His measured, ghostly footsteps follow you long into the night."},"E022.1":{"s":"You put the untouched supplies from the refectory into travel bags. Not a single candle goes out.","f":"In the corridor you can hear the steps of monks who have long since lost their lives, and the path to the exit is blocked by armed guards. A skirmish begins."},"E022.2":{"s":"Behind the darkened altar slab a cache of gold is discovered. The candle fire does not flicker while you take the loot.","f":"An old funeral seal is triggered in the treasury, severely wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The candles in the empty refectory continue to burn.","v":{"nf":"The funeral seal flares above the treasury, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The chest remains closed."}},"E022.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} performs the ritual, and the monastery candles begin to go out for the first time in many years. The party receives gold and supplies for the journey.","f":"{{heroName}} completes the prayer, but in the empty cells no answer or footsteps are heard. The ritual does not change the fate of the monastery."},"E022.4":{"s":"You leave the monastery's candles burning and its refectory untouched. Not a single living voice follows you out."},"E023.1":{"s":"The bone crown recognizes the authority of the King, and a cache of gold is revealed at the foot of the altar. The whispering stops.","f":"The crown clamps down on the King's head, and the curse kills him in an instant. The journey ends at the altar.","v":{"nf":"The bone crown is tightened on the King's head, but the killing curse does not work. The altar does not give rewards."}},"E023.2":{"s":"The crown does not harm the chosen hero, and gold is discovered at the altar. Whispers promise even more, but the party leaves.","f":"Bone teeth burn the one to whom the crown was given; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The whispering under the vaults does not subside.","v":{"nf":"Bone barbs flare, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The crown has to be removed."}},"E023.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} breaks the crown with a blessed blow, and the dark whisper disappears. Supplies are found in a niche behind the altar.","f":"The altar responds to the blow by awakening the bone guards. A skirmish begins."},"E023.4":{"s":"You leave the bone crown on its altar. Its whisper follows you, but no one looks back."},"E024.1":{"s":"The field treasurer's chest passes into your hands before the dead notice it's missing. The gold is sent to the treasury.","f":"The entire column halts at once, turning its helmets towards the thieves. A battle begins."},"E024.2":{"s":"You take the lagging soldier behind a rock ridge and take his travel coins.","f":"The dead man gives a silent signal, and the formation crumbles into armed pursuers. A skirmish begins."},"E024.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} makes a short raid on the tail of the column and manages to take the chest. It contains gold.","f":"One of the dead horsemen manages to strike the retreating ones; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The dead horseman cuts through the line of raiders, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The raid breaks down."}},"E024.4":{"s":"You wait out the march, motionless, until the last pair of dead boots disappears into the darkness. Not a single soldier turns his head."},"E025.1":{"s":"The spider-riding guide leads you through the canyon and, on parting, hands over a share of the provisions promised in your bargain.","f":"The road, which is too cheap, leads to a dark elf outpost, where they demand another payment. A skirmish begins."},"E025.2":{"s":"The guide reluctantly returns some of your coins when you insist on a written guarantee. The gold goes back into your treasury.","f":"The dark elf states that the guarantees are paid separately, and the party loses gold in fruitless negotiations."},"E025.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} spots the signal marks behind the guide's back and finds a safe detour. Along the way, you gather supplies.","f":"The guide recognizes the surveillance and signals an ambush among the rocks. A skirmish begins."},"E025.4":{"s":"You refuse a dangerously cheap guide. A giant spider quietly moves its paws while its owner looks for new clients."},"E026.1":{"s":"You pry a heavy shard from the crystal and sell it for gold at the nearest market. A dull crack echoes through the crevice.","f":"The crystal responds with a flash of dark light, severely wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The loot must be abandoned.","v":{"nf":"The obsidian crystal flashes with a dark light, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The fragment was not obtained."}},"E026.2":{"s":"The foundation crumbles, and valuable fragments remain among the rubble. The party takes the gold after selling the find.","f":"There is a deadly seal at the base; {{affectedHeroName}} dies when the crystal collapses.","v":{"nf":"The base of the crystal collapses, but no one among the available fighters dies. The broken stone remains under the seal."}},"E026.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} strengthens the crevice and safely removes the fragments. The party receives gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} notices that the crystal continues to grow under the securing beams and stops working. The reward remains unavailable."},"E026.4":{"s":"You walk past the crystal, leaving traces of someone else's prey untouched. The dark shine is visible for a long time between the rocks."},"E027.1":{"s":"The Assassin accepts your consent and transfers a golden advance for the execution of the contract.","f":"The hunt turns into a trap, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded. The Assassin disappears before an explanation can be demanded.","v":{"nf":"The contract results in a trap being set, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The Assassin disappears without explanation."}},"E027.2":{"s":"You manage to disarm the assassin and take the gold from him.","f":"The assassin escapes the grip and draws a second dagger. A skirmish begins."},"E027.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} offers the mercenary better conditions than the previous customer, and a new companion joins your party.","f":"The Assassin refuses to break the contract and hides in the darkness. The deal did not go through.","v":{"rs":"The mercenary accepts your better offer, but there is no room for him in your party. He leaves gold in thanks for the chance."}},"E027.4":{"s":"You post a guard and do not accept the mercenary's threat. Until dawn, no one sleeps peacefully in the camp, but no attack occurs."},"E028.1":{"s":"The purchase is weighed on dark elven scales and packed in a sealed bag. The party receives paid supplies."},"E028.2":{"s":"The prisoner is released after bargaining, and soon a new companion joins the party. The auctioneer is reluctant to issue a receipt.","v":{"rs":"The auction is over and the prisoner is released, but he is unable to join the party. In return he leaves gold."}},"E028.3":{"s":"Your bid wins the auction. The gold prize goes into your treasury.","f":"The bid fails and the auctioneer takes the agreed upon coins."},"E028.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} intercepts the trade negotiations, and some of the supplies are obtained without weapons.","f":"The auctioneer calls for armed security, deeming the intervention a threat to the market. A skirmish begins."},"E028.5":{"s":"You walk away beneath the black awnings, unwilling to take part in the trade in captives and provisions. The auctioneer's hammer sounds again behind you."},"E029.1":{"s":"The spider silk supports the weight of the party, and on the far side are the remaining supplies of the abandoned caravan.","f":"One of the threads breaks underfoot, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded when falling.","v":{"nf":"The silk thread breaks underfoot, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The crossing remains dangerous."}},"E029.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks each node and leads the rest to a safe shore. Among the abandoned carts are gold and supplies.","f":"Halfway across, the silk bridge gives way, gravely wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The abandoned caravan remains beyond your reach.","v":{"nf":"The silk bridge bows under the scout, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The caravan remains out of reach."}},"E029.3":{"s":"You cut the supporting threads behind your back, and the bridge settles into the abyss, leaving valuables on its side. The resulting gold replenishes the treasury.","f":"The bridge guards notice the cut and rush to stop the party. A skirmish begins."},"E029.4":{"s":"You take the long way around the chasm, using up supplies on the crossing. The abandoned caravan stays visible high above."},"E030.1":{"s":"The messenger gives the promised gold payment, but immediately points to the patrol that needs to be destroyed. A skirmish begins."},"E030.2":{"s":"You demand a higher payment, and the messenger hands over the gold before the skirmish begins.","f":"The envoy responds to the demand with an order to attack the royal party. The battle begins."},"E030.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} convinces both sides to enter into negotiations, and the envoy gives gold for the prevented raid.","f":"An attempt by {{heroName}} to change the route of the conflict fails, and the patrol meets you with weapons. A skirmish begins."},"E030.4":{"s":"You refuse the gold offered for attacking another party's patrol. The dark-elven messenger silently puts the coins away."},"E031.1":{"s":"You free the miners from beneath the fallen rock, and their crew rewards you with gold and supplies. The first man out insists on having his helmet back at once.","f":"The rubble is shifted too roughly, and a falling stone gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The stones in the blocked adit fall down, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The clearing is stopped."}},"E031.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} braces the shaft with strong supports and leads the miners to safety. Their crew rewards you with gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} finds a crack in the vault and stops work before it becomes deadly. Rescue is delayed."},"E031.3":{"s":"You take away boxes of valuable ore while the dwarves are busy with the collapse. The proceeds replenish the treasury.","f":"The miners notice the loss and rush in pursuit with heavy hammers. A skirmish begins."},"E031.4":{"s":"You call the neighboring team for help and do not risk people in the rubble. Dwarves give a modest gold payment for timely alarm."},"E032.1":{"s":"Your hammer hits the exact center of the target, and the manager reluctantly gives out the winnings in gold.","f":"The hammer makes a beautiful arc and misses the stone circle. The contributed coins remain with the organizers."},"E032.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} throws the hammer with such force that no one dares to argue about the result. The gnomes give out a gold reward.","f":"{{heroName}} hurls the hammer past the scoring ring. The organiser throws up his hands."},"E032.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} clips the handle when throwing, and the hammer bounces right into the scoring mark. The party gets the gold.","f":"{{heroName}}'s trick throw is ruled a foul, and the party must pay a penalty in gold."},"E032.4":{"s":"You remain spectators of the dwarven competition. The last hammer misses its target, but knocks someone's boot out of the ground."},"E033.1":{"s":"The convoy arrives at the fortress gates intact, and the dwarves pay for the protection with gold and supplies.","f":"Robbers appear on the road, noticing the weakened security. A skirmish begins."},"E033.2":{"s":"The elder dwarf gives the gold payment in advance, deciding not to argue with the armed party.","f":"The caravan's owner insists on seeing the job done before opening his purse. No agreement is reached."},"E033.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} notices traces of an ambush before the convoy enters the gorge. The dwarves give thanks for safe passage with gold and supplies.","f":"Despite the reconnaissance of {{heroName}}, the attack begins from the other side of the road. There's a skirmish ahead."},"E033.4":{"s":"You lead the dwarven convoy off the road and take some of the supplies before the owners come to their senses.","f":"The guards of the convoy gather together and raise the alarm throughout the valley. The battle begins."},"E034.1":{"s":"The dwarven door yields to blows, and behind it lies gold. The rune light on the stone fades.","f":"The hidden seal hits those who break the door, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The safe responds to the breach with a flash of a protective seal, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The door remains closed."}},"E034.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} parses the sequence of signs and opens the safe without noise. The gold found goes to the treasury.","f":"One of the runes changes order right during the reading, and the party loses supplies during an urgent retreat."},"E034.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} stops the security mechanism and allows you to open the door without risk. There is gold inside.","f":"The protective rune triggers on the last lock and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The last rune flares as the lock is disabled, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The vault stays shut."}},"E034.4":{"s":"You leave the dwarven door and its warnings untouched. Around the bend, the sound of rune buzzing finally disappears."},"E035.1":{"s":"The engineer restarts the machine, wipes the oil from his hands and shares his travelling provisions.","f":"During testing, a new part breaks, for which the mechanic demands compensation in gold."},"E035.2":{"s":"The dwarf hands you the paid supplies and immediately returns to dismantling his stubborn engine."},"E035.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} adjusts the power unit, and the machine roars to life with a deafening clang. The mechanic rewards you with supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} notices hidden wear and hesitates to start the unit until parts are replaced. The engineer remains at the car."},"E035.4":{"s":"The dwarf engineer becomes interested in the campaign and sends a new companion to the party, ready to help on the road.","f":"The mechanic refuses to leave the car unattended. He promises to think about it when he completes the repairs.","v":{"rs":"The engineer is willing to join your campaign, but there is no room for another fighter. Instead, he gives you gold."}},"E036.1":{"s":"You return the ancestral hammer to the elder. He studies the clan markings for a long moment before handing over the gold.","f":"The gang notices their pursuers at the pass and comes out to meet them with weapons. A skirmish begins."},"E036.2":{"s":"The elder gives the promised golden advance and demands the return of the ancestral hammer before the next full moon.","f":"The elder doubts your resolve and refuses your full advance. The party loses some gold during preparation."},"E036.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} intercepts the robbers on a narrow section of the pass and returns the hammer without a long chase. Dwarves pay in gold.","f":"The gang turns the entire convoy against the party, and the skirmish escalates into a battle."},"E036.4":{"s":"You refuse to take on someone else's ancestral debt. The elder tightens his grip on the empty belt loop where the hammer once hung."},"E037.1":{"s":"The demonic seal burns, opening the way to the bag of coins. The party gets the gold.","f":"A crimson sigil flashes beneath the chosen fighter, and {{affectedHeroName}} dies from the unleashed curse.","v":{"nf":"The Red Seal releases a killing curse, but none of the available fighters are killed. The symbol remains dangerous."}},"E037.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} destroys the rune in the correct sequence and gains access to gold and supplies.","f":"One misread symbol responds with a blow of dark power; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The misread rune responds with a blow of dark power, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The seal is not broken."}},"E037.3":{"s":"The blood price is paid: {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded, and the crimson seal releases its pouch of coins. The party gains gold at a bitter cost."},"E037.4":{"s":"You leave a burning sign on a stone and pass by. The bag of coins continues to wait for a new person."},"E038.1":{"s":"The demon accepts the gold and politely puts the paid supplies into a travel bag. There are three blank lines at the bottom of the contract."},"E038.2":{"s":"The demon smiles and pays out a fortune in gold. To your surprise, every coin is real.","f":"The hidden price of the bargain comes due, and demonic magic gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The demonic desire comes with a hidden cost, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The merchant remains at the table."}},"E038.3":{"s":"The condition is met: a new companion joins your party.","f":"Instead of an ally, the demon releases armed opponents from the seal. A skirmish begins.","v":{"rs":"The wish merchant promises an ally, but the party has nowhere to accept him. Instead of a recruit, he gives out gold."}},"E038.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} rewrites the contract so that the demon himself pays you gold for early termination.","f":"The demon finds a counter-penalty in the new edition, and the party loses some of the gold."},"E038.5":{"s":"You refuse to make a wish whose price remains unknown. The demon closes his book, smiling as if he has taken no offence."},"E039.1":{"s":"You break the chains around the circle of fire, and the freed demon joins your party.","f":"The demon rushes at the liberators before he can pronounce the oath. A skirmish begins.","v":{"rs":"The demon is free, but there is no room for him in the party. He leaves gold in thanks for the broken chains."}},"E039.2":{"s":"The demon takes an oath before the chains are removed, and a new ally joins the party; gold remains in the circle.","f":"The demon does not want to swear before being freed and breaks the chains with rage. The battle begins.","v":{"rs":"The demon takes an oath, but the party cannot accept a new fighter. Instead of service, he hands over gold."}},"E039.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} changes the seal of submission, and the circle of fire releases a new companion under your banner.","f":"The rune of submission responds with a flash, seriously wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The demon remains in the circle.","v":{"rs":"The binding seal has been rewritten, but there is no room for the liberated demon. He rewards you with gold.","nf":"The Fire Rune explodes when rewritten, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The demon remains inside the circle."}},"E039.4":{"s":"You strengthen the chains and take the offerings left at the circle. Gold goes to the treasury.","f":"The spell rejects the new bindings. You retreat, leaving the offerings untouched."},"E040.1":{"s":"The party quickly walks across the hot coals before the demonic fires can close.","f":"{{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded on a hot road, and the others have to pull him aside.","v":{"nf":"The hot road burns soles and shields, but none of the available fighters is gravely wounded. Direct passage is stopped."}},"E040.2":{"s":"You cover your soles and wheels with supplies, prepared for the dangerous journey. The party passes the coal road, saving people."},"E040.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} raises the shields in a dense wall, and the party passes through the heat, preserving supplies.","f":"A shield glows red-hot, gravely wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The party must abandon the crossing.","v":{"nf":"The shield becomes red hot, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The party retreats from the fiery road."}},"E040.4":{"s":"You turn onto a long path off the coal road. The detour costs some of the supplies."},"E041.1":{"s":"You understand the whispers from the crevice and find the old hiding place indicated by them. Gold replenishes the treasury.","f":"The voices lead the party to empty stones and fall silent; supplies are wasted on a useless path."},"E041.2":{"s":"Deep in the crevice you find coins that have not been touched by light for hundreds of years. The gold goes to the treasury.","f":"The old crevice closes underfoot, and {{affectedHeroName}} dies in the darkness.","v":{"nf":"The crevice closes around the explorers, but none of the eligible fighters dies. You must abandon the search."}},"E041.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} forces voices to reveal the location of the hiding place and a safe exit. The party takes gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} pronounces an order, but in response only his own echo sounds. The mystery remains below."},"E041.4":{"s":"You seal the chasm, and the whispering finally stops. Among the stones, a small gold payment is discovered, left by previous travelers."},"E042.1":{"s":"The king signs in blood, and the demon counts out the gold and gives out supplies. The seal of the agreement remains on the skin.","f":"The demon accepts the signature, but the oath turns out to be fatal: the King dies. The journey ends.","v":{"nf":"The oath flares with deadly magic, yet the King survives. The demon gains no claim on his life."}},"E042.2":{"s":"The signature of another hero is accepted instead of the royal one, and the demon pays the promised gold.","f":"The agreement leaves a cursed mark on the signatory; {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The cursed signature leaves its mark, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The bargain yields nothing."}},"E042.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a clause in the demonic contract and turns it against the owner himself. The party takes the gold.","f":"The demon recognizes the deception and calls his guards. A skirmish begins."},"E042.4":{"s":"You refuse to sign even the most tempting agreement in blood. The demon carefully folds the sheet, assuring that the offer is still valid."},"E043.1":{"s":"You give the wounded angel supplies and cover his broken wing. In parting, he thanks the party with gold."},"E043.2":{"s":"The party guards the angel until dawn, preventing marauders from approaching him. In gratitude you receive supplies.","f":"Night light attracts predators faster than protection can be organized. A skirmish begins."},"E043.3":{"s":"The angel considers your proposal, and soon a new companion appears in the party.","f":"The angel thanks for the invitation, but cannot leave the road until the wing is restored. The party leaves without replenishment.","v":{"rs":"The angel agrees to go next to the King, but there is no place in the party. He leaves gold instead of service."}},"E043.4":{"s":"{{heroName}} repairs the seal of light, concealing the angel from prying eyes. In gratitude, he gives you gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} discovers that the seal is too damaged and requires materials that are not currently available. The angel remains waiting for help."},"E044.1":{"s":"The angelic judge accepts the deposit and returns the gold coins after verification. The road is open again."},"E044.2":{"s":"The judge recognizes your right to leave, although he does not hide his disapproval. The party moves on.","f":"The angelic guard declares refusal to be resistance to judgment. A skirmish begins."},"E044.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} proves that the party does not have any stolen goods, and the judge returns the disputed gold.","f":"The judge rejects the arguments and imposes a fine; the party loses part of the gold."},"E044.4":{"s":"You are the first to draw your weapon, and the angelic guard accepts the challenge. The battle begins.","f":"The guards do not respond to the first attack and let the party pass, considering the dispute to be settled."},"E045.1":{"s":"The bell answers the question with a shining blast, which reveals surviving supplies in the ruins.","f":"The ringing becomes a blast of light, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded on the chapel steps.","v":{"nf":"Sky Bell responds with a strike of light, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The ringing stops."}},"E045.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} performs the prescribed ritual and hears a clear bell response. It is possible to find supplies among the ruins.","f":"{{heroName}} pronounces the words of the ritual, but the bell remains silent. Nobody gets an answer."},"E045.3":{"s":"You remove the silver plates from the bell and receive gold for them.","f":"Pilgrims notice an attempt to dismantle the shrine and rush to protect the bell. A skirmish begins."},"E045.4":{"s":"You leave the bell on the ruined chapel and don't ask it a question. A barely audible, lonely ringing sound is heard from behind."},"E046.1":{"s":"The guardian acknowledges that you asked with dignity and grants you some of the celestial metal. Its sale brings gold to your treasury.","f":"The angel listens to the request and leaves the crater under guard. The party has to leave without finding anything."},"E046.2":{"s":"You pass the custodian's test and gain the right to take away the valuable metal. Gold from its sale replenishes the treasury.","f":"The test turns out to be too harsh, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The test at the fallen star ends with a dangerous blow, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The guard does not recognize success."}},"E046.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} accepts a fair fight and deserves a share of the fallen star. The found metal turns into gold.","f":"The Guardian is faster than expected and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded during the test.","v":{"nf":"The Fallen Star Guardian outpaces the duelist, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The duel of honor is stopped."}},"E046.4":{"s":"At night, you manage to pick up part of the heavenly metal without waking the guard. Gold replenishes the treasury.","f":"The angel notices the loss and raises his warriors. The battle begins."},"E047.1":{"s":"The choir soothes the tired companions, and the pilgrims share supplies.","f":"A false voice disrupts the chant, and the party loses some of its supplies in the confusion."},"E047.2":{"s":"You unmask the false chorister and receive a reward in gold.","f":"The substitute singer tears off his mask and calls for armed accomplices. A skirmish begins."},"E047.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} recognizes someone else's note in a common prayer and exposes the substitution without a fight. The choir thanks you with gold and supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} hears the wrong voice, but its source disappears among the ruins. The singing continues."},"E047.4":{"s":"You leave the ruins of the angelic choir behind. Even in the distance, one false voice clearly hurts the ear."},"E048.1":{"s":"The envoy accepts the gold in payment of someone else's debt, and the persecuted person is released. A new companion joins your party.","v":{"rs":"You pay another's debt and set the captive free, but there is no room for him in your party. He rewards you with gold."}},"E048.2":{"s":"You vouch for a person without payment and seek forgiveness of the debt; a new companion appears in the party.","f":"The envoy demands a material guarantee, and the party is deprived of part of the gold.","v":{"rs":"The debt is forgiven, but the freed man has no place among the King’s companions. He leaves the gold as surety."}},"E048.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} proposes service in place of debt, and the envoy accepts the bargain as fair. A new companion joins the party, bringing supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} fails to convince the envoy that service can be considered repayment of a debt. The debtor remains under supervision.","v":{"rs":"The envoy accepts the new terms, but there is no room for the debtor in your party. Instead of a recruit, you receive gold."}},"E048.4":{"s":"You do not interfere in someone else's litigation. The angelic messenger returns to the agreement, and the man by the road silently awaits the decision."},"E049.1":{"s":"You find an animal trail and help the patrol clear the pass. Draconids pay in gold.","f":"The trail leads straight to an occupied lair, where danger is closer than expected. A skirmish begins."},"E049.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a safe path through the claw marks and leads the patrol to the desired path. As a reward, the party receives gold and supplies.","f":"The beast rushes out of the smoky crevice, severely wounding {{affectedHeroName}} before retreating.","v":{"nf":"The beast attacks from a smoky crevice, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The trail is lost."}},"E049.3":{"s":"The party reaches the lair and returns with evidence that the pass is safe again. The patrol gives out gold.","f":"Instead of a single creature, the lair holds an entire pack. The search erupts into a battle."},"E049.4":{"s":"You take the long road around the closed pass and use up some of your supplies. The Draconid patrol remains to search for the beast."},"E050.1":{"s":"You withstand the heat of the sacred chalice and receive a golden reward from the draconians.","f":"The stone sears flesh, gravely wounding {{affectedHeroName}}. The trial is halted.","v":{"nf":"The heat of the bowl becomes unbearable, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The test has to be stopped."}},"E050.2":{"s":"{{heroName}} withstands the heat under the shield without retreating a single step. Draconids pay gold for endurance.","f":"The heat passes through the metal and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}. The test is stopped.","v":{"nf":"The heat passes through the shield, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The bowl is left by the stone."}},"E050.3":{"s":"You pay the gold and are freed from the test at the fiery cup. Draconids accept rejection without ridicule."},"E050.4":{"s":"The draconians listen to the ridicule and do not find a worthy answer, but you receive a golden bet.","f":"The offended guardians of the chalice take up arms. A skirmish begins."}});
export { OUTCOMES_EN_E001_E050 };
